WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.664 --> 00:00:05.960
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> Is there a New Year’s Eve that you always remember?

2
00:00:06.183 --> 00:00:12.434
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> Yes, it was when I was seventeen years old, so quite a long time ago.

3
00:00:12.463 --> 00:00:16.120
But it’s definitely my most memorable one.

4
00:00:16.981 --> 00:00:17.930
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> Where were you?

5
00:00:18.288 --> 00:00:22.903
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> Well, a friend invited me to Edinburgh for New Year’s Eve.

6
00:00:23.087 --> 00:00:32.240
I was still at school, but my friend, she was older than me, she was nineteen, and she was at university in Edinburgh.

7
00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:35.608
My parents didn’t want me to go, but in the end, they said OK.

8
00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:48.999
I was incredibly excited because ‘Hogmanay’, that’s what they call New Year’s Eve in Scotland, is the biggest celebration in,

9
00:00:49.086 --> 00:00:53.760
in Europe, I think, with thousands of people in the streets.

10
00:00:53.779 --> 00:00:55.501
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> So what happened?

11
00:00:55.695 --> 00:01:04.364
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> We decided to go and watch the fireworks from the top of Calton Hill, that’s a high point in the city where there’s a good view.

12
00:01:04.655 --> 00:01:11.873
My friend had a Norwegian flatmate, and she also had some friends staying, some Norwegian girls from Oslo.

13
00:01:12.221 --> 00:01:18.801
We all had a dinner first in their flat and then started walking to Calton Hill.

14
00:01:18.956 --> 00:01:24.200
It was cold, but not snowing or raining, which was good.

15
00:01:24.703 --> 00:01:30.296
The Norwegian girls bought some small fireworks, and started lighting them in the street,

16
00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:40.465
they said that’s typical in Norway, that people set off fireworks in the street, and suddenly one firework hit me in the face.

17
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:42.420
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> How awful!

18
00:01:42.449 --> 00:01:49.706
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> Yes, it was horrible, incredibly painful and for a few minutes, I couldn’t see at all.

19
00:01:49.754 --> 00:01:50.877
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> What did you do?

20
00:01:50.935 --> 00:02:01.259
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> Well, luckily there were ambulances driving round the city because actually quite a lot of people get injured in Edinburgh on New Year’s Eve,

21
00:02:01.472 --> 00:02:06.058
and my friends quickly found one and they went with me to hospital.

22
00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:14.651
The doctors looked at me, and it wasn’t too serious, but they put a big bandage on my face, and over one eye.

23
00:02:14.738 --> 00:02:17.515
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> So where were you at midnight?

24
00:02:17.747 --> 00:02:23.862
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> Well, we were still at the hospital, so we never celebrated Hogmanay properly.

25
00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.274
I didn’t phone my parents, because there was nothing they could do,

26
00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:38.879
but when I went home the next day and they saw my face, they were really shocked and angry because somehow they thought it was my fault!

27
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:47.820
But some weeks later my friends came down to London and we had a fantastic party to make up for missing New Year’s Eve.